LlamaServerProvider.cs:393-396:
    while (!reader.EndOfStream)
    {
        ct.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();
        var line = await reader.ReadLineAsync(ct);
Same pattern at OllamaProvider.cs:220, AnthropicProvider.cs:246 and 496 (`while (!streamEnded && !reader.EndOfStream)`), OpenAiProvider.cs:113, GeminiProvider.cs:202. `StreamReader.EndOfStream` performs a SYNCHRONOUS blocking Read() when its buffer is empty (this is analyzer rule CA2024: 'Do not use StreamReader.EndOfStream in async methods'). It takes no CancellationToken, and HttpClient.Timeout does not cover body reads after HttpCompletionOption.ResponseHeadersRead. The consumer runs on the UI thread: ChatViewModel.cs:2156 `await foreach (var token in _agentService.ChatStreamAsync(history, input, ct))` and ChatViewModel.cs:1743 `await _agentService.ExecuteAgenticAsync(...)` โ€” the whole project has exactly ONE ConfigureAwait(false) (SubAgentService), so every async-iterator continuation resumes on the WPF dispatcher.

AgentToolService.cs:1627-1632:
    string stdout, stderr;
    try
    {
        await process.WaitForExitAsync(cts.Token);
        stdout = await process.StandardOutput.ReadToEndAsync(cts.Token);
        stderr = await process.StandardError.ReadToEndAsync(cts.Token);
Both pipes are redirected (lines 1612-1613) but nothing drains them until the process exits. A child that writes more than the ~4KB anonymous-pipe buffer blocks on write and never exits โ’ WaitForExitAsync only returns when cts fires โ’ Kill + `return Fail(call, $"Command timed out ({timeoutMs / 1000}s limit)")`. Compare the CORRECT concurrent pattern the codebase itself uses elsewhere: ExecutePowerShellAsync (AgentToolService.cs:3629-3631), HookService.cs:294-296, GitService.cs:444-446 ('If we await WaitForExitAsync first, the process may block filling the pipe buffer'). Reached by run_build (ExecuteRunBuildAsync:1461, timeout_ms=180000), run_tests (1482, 300000), and RunVerifyBuildAsync:1504 โ€” and AutoVerifyAfterEditEnabled defaults TRUE (AppSettings.cs:133), so it fires after every successful edit turn (CodeAgentService.cs:1958-1969).

findings.fix:
Reorder to the concurrent-read pattern already used three other places in this codebase:
    var stdoutTask = process.StandardOutput.ReadToEndAsync(cts.Token);
    var stderrTask = process.StandardError.ReadToEndAsync(cts.Token);
    await process.WaitForExitAsync(cts.Token);
    stdout = await stdoutTask; stderr = await stderrTask;
